schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "Building Your Founding Team"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  high_risk: true
  summary: >-
    A guide for organizers standing up a local ReFi node on assembling a
    small, durable founding team. Argues to start with two or three
    committed people rather than a crowd, fill roles (convener,
    builder/doer, treasurer/ops) rather than titles, bring people in through
    real work rather than abstract membership, and design against burnout
    from day one (no single point of failure, legitimate rest). Cites named
    real-world nodes (ReFi Medellín, ReFi Cartagena) and their named founders
    as worked examples, plus research on founder conflict and DAO burnout.
  audience: organizers standing up a local ReFi/regen node
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      recruiting a crowd feels like momentum but the article argues small,
      trust-bonded founding teams (2-3 people) outperform larger, looser
      ones that "attended one call."
    - >-
      one person can hold two of the three core roles at the start, but the
      article warns against any one person holding all three for long —
      tension between fast bootstrapping and burnout risk.
  related_concepts:
    - node-founding-team-roles
  related_resources:
    - ReFi Medellín
    - ReFi Cartagena
    - Safe (multisig wallets)
    - ReFi DAO Local Node Incubator
  maturity: raw
  public_use: requires-community-consent
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/building-founding-team.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-f2680cdb2876
  source_lineage: building-founding-team.md
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - Individual named organizers (Tereza Bízková, Juan Giraldo, Daniela,
      Ximena, Diana Monclou, Fabio Anaya) are NOT modeled as public
      person-nodes per the ingest skill's high-risk rule. They are referenced
      only inside the ReFi Medellín / ReFi Cartagena resource objects and the
      companion public-use-boundary object, all already publicly named in the
      article's own cited sources (a public interview, a public grant
      report).
    - high_risk: true set on this entry because it (a) names real community
      organizers by name/role and (b) gives governance/structural
      recommendations (multisig signer counts, role design) for
      funds-and-leadership decisions — both are ingest-skill high-risk
      triggers. See the public-use-boundary object for the review gate.
